NEARS-1147 QA — TASK BUG (low, does NOT break an AC)
"ModuleIdDriftFixtureTest asserts EXACT violation lists, so any ambient drift makes the fixture
 suite fail with a misleading diagnosis."

tests/Feature/ModuleIdDriftFixtureTest.php:41,56,77
    $this->assertSame([self::ITEM_ID], $report['violations_a']);

arrangeCleanBaseline() only repairs the 7 NEARS-1074 ids. Any OTHER ambient violation (e.g. the
QA1132-* rows a concurrent session committed) is NOT repaired, so these three cases fail with:

    Failed asserting that two arrays are identical.
    -Array &0 [0 => 16]
    +Array &0 [0 => 16, 1 => 41316, 2 => 41426]

That is a confusing signal: the fixture suite's job is "the corruption I planted is NAMED", not
"my row is the only violation in the database" — the latter is ModuleIdDriftGuardTest's job, and it
already fails correctly in that situation. Result: one real condition, two alarms, one of them
pointing at the wrong thing.

Suggested: assert containment (assertContains(self::ITEM_ID, $report['violations_a'])) plus the
exit code, and leave exactness to the ambient net.

Impact: none on the ACs — AC2 was demonstrated live and green on an uncontaminated DB. Filed for
signal quality, not correctness.
